# Project Conventions

## Tech Stack

- Frontend: React + TypeScript + Vite
- Desktop: Tauri (Rust backend, native webview)
- Storage: localStorage (web) / Tauri FS plugin (desktop)
- HTTP: Vite proxy (web) / Tauri HTTP plugin (desktop)

## Platform Awareness

- Use `isTauri()` from `src/utils/platform.ts` to detect desktop vs web.
- Use `httpFetch()` from `src/utils/httpClient.ts` for all HTTP requests.
- Use async functions from `src/utils/storage.ts` for all persistence.
- Never use `localStorage` directly — always go through the storage abstraction.

## Key Files

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `src/App.tsx` | Main app, routing, global state |
| `src/pages/EnvironmentManager.tsx` | Unified env/microservice/auth config page |
| `src/utils/storage.ts` | Dual-mode persistence layer |
| `src/utils/tauriStore.ts` | Tauri file-system storage |
| `src/utils/httpClient.ts` | Dual-mode HTTP client |
| `src/utils/platform.ts` | Platform detection |
| `src/utils/requestTree.ts` | Requests tree manipulation with safe insert helpers |
| `src/utils/requestUrlResolver.ts` | Base URL resolution for multi-env collections |
| `src/utils/requestAuthState.ts` | Auth config ↔ UI state mapping |
| `src/utils/catalogExport.ts` | Catalog → Requests export transformation |
| `src/engine/executor.ts` | HTTP test execution engine |
| `src-tauri/tauri.conf.json` | Tauri app config |
| `scripts/version.sh` | Version bump script |

## Naming

- App name: **RedfireForge**
- Tagline: **Redfire Performance Workbench**
- Desktop title bar: "RedfireForge — Redfire Performance Workbench"
- Export filenames: `{env}-{microservice}-{level}-{name}-{timestamp}.json`
